cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the paper describing it."
title: "MLdpit: machine learning downscaled precipitation in time"
abstract: >-
  MLdpit performs temporal downscaling of precipitation, converting hourly
  fields into 10-minute fields with a four-level U-Net. A softmax over the six
  output channels yields sub-hourly fractions that are multiplied by the hourly
  total, so the six 10-minute fields sum to the hourly field from which they
  were derived, to within float32 rounding. The released model was trained on
  ICON simulations over a 501 x 501 grid at ~3 km resolution.
